WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.980
Is that glowing speck inside the cell, or just sitting behind it?

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.960
Under an ordinary microscope, thick glowing tissue turns hazy.

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.460
Light from layers above and below floods the lens at once, collapsing depth into one

4
00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:16.460
flat blur.

5
00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.367
A confocal microscope clears that blur with a pinhole.

6
00:00:23.827 --> 00:00:29.107
Fluorescent dyes or antibodies make chosen structures glow as a focused laser scans

7
00:00:29.107 --> 00:00:34.927
one depth. Light from the focal spot comes back to a point, right at the pinhole.

8
00:00:36.227 --> 00:00:40.587
Light from other depths is spread wide there, so most hits the barrier around it.

9
00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:46.410
Rejecting out-of-focus light with a pinhole yields a sharp optical section.

10
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.390
It slices thick tissue with light instead of a blade.

11
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:56.270
Step the focus deeper through intact tissue to collect a stack of clean slices.

12
00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:02.090
Software rebuilds that stack in three dimensions, showing where every labelled

13
00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:03.090
structure sits.

14
00:01:03.983 --> 00:01:05.563
Test that on our green cell.

15
00:01:06.923 --> 00:01:10.043
A red speck sits just above the cell, touching its outside.

16
00:01:11.343 --> 00:01:13.723
In a flat image, red overlaps green.

17
00:01:15.103 --> 00:01:18.963
When you step through a confocal stack, how can you tell the speck is outside?

18
00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:29.827
The speck peaks in a higher slice, outside the rebuilt cell, so software removes it.

19
00:01:31.247 --> 00:01:36.667
Raw volume misleads too: large cells hold more from size alone, so researchers

20
00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.727
divide internal label volume by cell volume.

21
00:01:40.987 --> 00:01:42.507
Independent checks show uptake.

22
00:01:44.167 --> 00:01:49.367
Label overlaps stained digestive compartments, which are acidic, so a dye that glows

23
00:01:49.367 --> 00:01:50.887
only in acid lights up.

24
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.170
Two limits remain.

25
00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:59.550
Fixed tissue, chemically preserved, captures one frozen moment, and seeing a

26
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.370
structure does not prove how it works.

27
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:08.070
Counting stained branches can mislead too: one nerve cell branches widely, so

28
00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:10.110
counting endings does not count neurons.

29
00:02:11.283 --> 00:02:14.703
Those guards let confocal imaging open thick tissue.

30
00:02:16.023 --> 00:02:22.423
In 2004, Polsky, Mel and Schiller imaged thin dendrites, a neuron's input branches,

31
00:02:22.723 --> 00:02:24.423
in rat neocortex slices.

32
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.743
They stimulated two sites, alone, then together.

33
00:02:30.043 --> 00:02:35.323
On one branch, nearby sites combined in an S-shape: slow, then steep, then level.

34
00:02:36.663 --> 00:02:41.103
Distant inputs simply added, supporting thin branches as separate subunits.

35
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:48.780
In 2007, Baluk and colleagues imaged intact sheets of mouse trachea to see how fluid

36
00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:49.880
enters lymph vessels.

37
00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:56.400
In the first, blind-ended vessels, cells were joined by short buttons, about 3.2

38
00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:00.780
micrometres long. Loose flaps lay between them.

39
00:03:02.160 --> 00:03:05.740
Larger collecting vessels had continuous, zipper-like junctions.

40
00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.940
From that structure alone, they proposed fluid enters between buttons.

41
00:03:12.033 --> 00:03:17.453
In 2012, Schafer and colleagues dyed each eye's nerve endings a different colour in

42
00:03:17.453 --> 00:03:23.013
young mice. They rebuilt green microglia, brain immune cells, in the visual

43
00:03:23.013 --> 00:03:29.953
thalamus. Pieces of those endings sat inside digestive compartments, relatively more

44
00:03:29.953 --> 00:03:31.053
from a silenced eye.

45
00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:36.933
By rejecting blur, one pinhole turns crowded tissue into measurable space.
